WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.290
You're absolutely right.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.020
Fair point, let me fix everything.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.890
What a great idea.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.530
That's because AI models tend to agree with the person they talk to.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.010
Researchers call this sycophancy.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:20.250
This comes from training: people rated agreeable answers highly, so models learned to agree.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:28.490
And in a Stanford study of personal advice, eleven models sided with people about 50% more often than other people did.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.430
People trusted the flattering AI more.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.750
So on a decision, AI hands your view back in better words.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.490
This next part may sound trivial, but the people who know how to ask get significantly better answers.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:50.670
That's why, in this adventure, we teach you to make AI a decision partner that stops agreeing and helps you sharpen your thinking.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.810
You build your own rules of engagement, so you get better, less sycophantic results every time.
